# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.local
.env.production

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Runtime data
pids
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# Coverage reports
coverage/

# Build folders
dist/
build/

# Cache
.cache/
.npm/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# VS Code
.vscode/

# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# ESLint cache
.eslintcache

# Prettier cache
.prettier-cache

# Package lock (optional, keep if your team tracks it)
# package-lock.json


- node_modules/ prevents thousands of installed packages from being uploaded to GitHub.
- .env protects sensitive information such as database connection strings and API keys.
- coverage/ excludes test coverage reports.
- .vscode/ and .idea/ exclude personal IDE settings.
- *.log prevents log files from cluttering the repository.
- dist/ and build/ exclude generated application files.

Evidence for Report:

1. .gitignore file in the GitHub repository.
2. node_modules not appearing in the repository.
3. .env excluded from commits.
4. A commit message such as:
                Add .gitignore and repository configuration

This demonstrates proper Git repository management practices for the SkillsTrack Student Support project
